What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltage0_band
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the RF output band selection. The ADMV1355 has two
		internal RF signal paths (low band and high band) selected by
		this attribute. No standard IIO attribute maps to internal
		band-path routing.
		Valid values: low_band high_band

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/out_altvoltage0_band_available
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of available RF band selections.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage0_mode
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the IF input operating mode. The ADMV1355 supports
		four mixer modes with different intermediate frequency input
		configurations. This selects which internal IF path is active.
		No standard IIO channel type covers device-specific mixer mode
		selection.
		Valid values: baseband complex_if_low complex_if_high if_hybrid

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage0_mode_available
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of available IF input modes.

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_sideband
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		Read/write the mixer sideband selection. Controls whether the
		lower sideband (LSB) or upper sideband (USB) of the mixer
		output is selected. This is a fundamental mixer topology control
		with no standard IIO mapping.
		Valid values: LSB USB

What:		/sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:deviceX/in_altvoltage1_sideband_available
KernelVersion:
Contact:	linux-iio@vger.kernel.org
Description:
		List of available mixer sideband selections.
